cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "vigiTwin: duplicate adjudication for pharmacovigilance reports"
abstract: >-
  A duplicate adjudication pipeline for pharmacovigilance adverse event reports,
  with the evaluation framework used to measure its performance. Report pairs
  flagged as suspected duplicates by an upstream candidate-generation method are
  classified as Duplicates, Otherwise related, Unrelated, or Abstain by a
  transparent rule-based decision logic combining rarity-based matching
  evidence, structured and clinical-date inconsistency signals, LLM-derived
  narrative signals, and explicit inter-report links.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Norén"
    given-names: "G. Niklas"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4595-230X"
    affiliation: "Uppsala Monitoring Centre"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-13"
license: "Apache-2.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24198670"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Uppsala-Monitoring-Centre/vigiTwin"
keywords:
  - pharmacovigilance
  - duplicate detection
  - record linkage
  - adverse drug reactions
  - large language models

# The `doi` above is the Zenodo *concept* DOI: it always resolves to the latest
# archived release, so it stays correct without being edited at each release and
# is the one the README badge points at. Zenodo also mints a per-release version
# DOI — v1.0.0 is 10.5281/zenodo.24198671 — which is what a reader should
# cite when reproducing a specific result. Do not swap the concept DOI for one
# here; `version:` above already says which release this file describes.

